From 989d1b155defbc936d82fc7252fd543e081dc641 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carson Daniel <wcarsond@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:17:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] vulkan: GGML_TYPE_Q12H - dequant shader, get_rows and a
 fused mat-vec

types.glsl gets block_q12h (412 bytes, QUANT_K 256, QUANT_R 1) and
dequant_funcs.glsl the reconstruction: ix from the nibble pair, bits =
(sm>>7)<<15 | lut[ix]<<7 | (sm&0x7F), f32 = bits<<16. The exception loop
breaks on epos[s] == 0xFF exactly like dequantize_row_q12h() on the CPU, so
the GPU and CPU agree bit for bit. get_dm returns (1,0) - Q12H has no scale.

"q12h" in type_names gives the generic mul_mat_vec.comp, get_rows_quant.comp
and the new dequant_q12h.comp (4 blocks per 256-thread workgroup). Q12H gets
no mul_mm shader, so big matmuls take the dequant-to-f16 path via
ggml_vk_get_to_fp16, while decode runs the fused mat-vec.

test-backend-ops: GGML_TYPE_Q12H in all_types and other_types. 13 q12h
MUL_MAT cases (n = 1..9, 64; k = 256, 4096), 2288/2288 passed on Vulkan1.

Greedy output on Qwen3-1.7B, -n 64 --temp 0 --seed 1, is byte-identical
across bf16/Vulkan1, q12h/Vulkan1, q12h/CPU, q12h/Vulkan0 and bf16/Vulkan0.
Vulkan0 is the Intel iGPU, which oneAPI/Level-Zero cannot see at all.
